---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Why French Gray Sea Salt · Purest Electrolyte"
  description="Most electrolytes use cheap table salt. We use French gray sea salt — naturally harvested, rich in 85+ trace minerals your body actually needs."
>
  <section class="container py-14 md:py-20 max-w-3xl">

    <a href="/about" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground mb-8 inline-block">← Back to About</a>

    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight mb-6">Why French Gray Sea Salt?</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground mb-12 leading-relaxed">
      Most electrolyte drinks use cheap, processed table salt. We don't. We use <strong>French gray sea salt</strong> — and the difference is profound.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-12">

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-3">What is French Gray Sea Salt?</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          French gray sea salt (sel gris) is hand-harvested from the Atlantic coast of France using traditional methods that date back over a thousand years. Unlike refined table salt, it's never bleached, never processed, and never stripped of its natural mineral content. It gets its distinctive gray color from the clay-lined salt ponds it's harvested from — and that clay is part of what makes it so special.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-3">85+ Trace Minerals — Not Just Sodium</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Table salt is essentially pure sodium chloride — two minerals. French gray sea salt naturally contains <strong>over 85 trace minerals</strong> including magnesium, potassium, calcium, zinc, iron, and many more. These aren't added artificially — they're naturally present because the salt was never refined away from them.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Your body doesn't just need sodium when you sweat. It loses a complex cocktail of minerals. French gray sea salt replenishes them the way nature intended.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-3">Table Salt vs. French Gray Sea Salt</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-secondary">
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-medium"></th>
                <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-medium">Table Salt</th>
                <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-medium text-foreground">French Gray Sea Salt</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground">Minerals</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">2 (Na + Cl)</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">85+</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground">Processing</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Heavily refined, bleached</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Hand-harvested, unrefined</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground">Anti-caking agents</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Yes</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">None</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground">Color</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Pure white (bleached)</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Natural gray (mineral-rich clay)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground">Absorption</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Sodium only</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Full mineral spectrum</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-3">Why It Matters for Hydration</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Proper hydration isn't just about water — it's about electrolyte balance. When you sweat, exercise at altitude, or spend time in the heat, your body loses far more than sodium. It loses magnesium (muscle function), potassium (heart rhythm), calcium (nerve signaling), and dozens of other trace minerals.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Replacing only sodium — like most sports drinks do — leaves the rest of your body under-resourced. French gray sea salt replenishes the full spectrum naturally, without synthetic additions or chemical processing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-3">Pam's Story</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          "I ended up in the hospital with hyponatremia — dangerous low sodium — even though I was drinking water constantly. I started researching what my body actually needed, and I kept coming back to French gray sea salt. It was the one ingredient that made everything make sense. That's why it's the foundation of every Purest product."
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">— Pam, Founder of Purest Electrolyte</p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-border">
      <a
        href="/products"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-foreground text-background px-8 py-3 text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity"
      >
        Shop Purest Electrolyte →
      </a>
    </div>

  </section>
</Layout>
